{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "```python\ndef change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    \"\"\"\n    if x == 0:\n        return '0'\n\n    result = []\n    is_negative = False\n    if x < 0:\n        is_negative = True\n        x = abs(x)\n\n    while x > 0:\n        remainder = x % base\n        result.append(str(remainder))\n        x //= base\n\n    if is_negative:\n        result.append('-')\n\n    return ''.join(result[::-1])\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence iteratively.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    if n == 2:\n        return 2\n    if n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the sequence with base cases for n=0, 1, 2, 3\n    fib_sequence = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    # Calculate subsequent elements using the iterative formula\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = fib_sequence[i-1] + fib_sequence[i-2] + fib_sequence[i-3] + fib_sequence[i-4]\n        fib_sequence.append(next_fib)\n\n    return fib_sequence[n]\n```"}
