{"task_id": "HumanEval/55", "solution": "```python\ndef fib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Return n-th Fibonacci number.\n    The sequence starts with F(1)=1, F(2)=1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n    if n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 1, 1\n    for _ in range(3, n + 1):\n        next_fib = a + b\n        a = b\n        b = next_fib\n    return b\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/56", "solution": "```python\ndef correct_bracketing(brackets: str):\n    \"\"\" brackets is a string of \"<\" and \">\".\n    return True if every opening bracket has a corresponding closing bracket.\n    \"\"\"\n    balance = 0\n    for char in brackets:\n        if char == '<':\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == '>':\n            balance -= 1\n        else:\n            # Handle invalid characters based on NFR2.\n            return False\n\n        # A negative balance means a closing bracket appeared without an open one.\n        if balance < 0:\n            return False\n\n    # For correct bracketing, the final balance must be zero.\n    return balance == 0\n```"}
